ul calculation. The engine suggests Nxe4 Bxe4 Nd2 Bb7. } 6. Nxe4 { White recaptures with Nxe4, restoring material balance. This immediate recapture keeps Black from consolidating extra material, though it's worth noting the prior **pin** context. The engine suggests Bxe4 Nd2 Bb7 e4. } 6... Bxe4 { Black recaptures with Bxe4, restoring material balance immediately. This prevents White from consolidating extra material, following up on the earlier **pin** on f3. The engine's best line is Nd2 Bb7 e4 Be7. } 7. Nd2 $1 { White creates an immediate threat with Nd2, putting the bishop on e4 under pressure. This forces Black to respond instead of improving freely, with Bb7 e4 Be7 Bd3 suggested by the engine. } 7... Bg6 { Black solves an immediate problem by moving the bishop to g6, rescuing it from danger. Good defensive moves like this also maintain overall position coordination. The engine suggests g3 Nc6 e3 a5. } 8. g3 { White reinforces the pawn chain with g3, creating a solid structural foundation. This chain controls key squares and restricts Black's piece activity, according to the engine's best line of Nc6 e3 a5 Bg2. } 8... Nc6 $6 { Black creates an immediate threat with Nc6, putting the pawn under pressure. This pawn has no safe retreat or counter-threat, so it must find a defender or fall; the engine suggests e3 a5 Bg2 Be7. } 9. e3 $1 { White solves an immediate problem with e3, rescuing the pawn from danger. Such defensive moves not only survive the moment but also keep the position coordinated. The engine suggests a5 Bg2 Be7 Nb1. } 9... a6 { Black advances to a6, a strategic move that often prevents White's pieces from reaching b5 or prepares queenside expansion. White's f2-g3 pawn chain maintains control over key central squares, shaping the strategic landscape. The engine suggests Bg2 h5 h4 b5. } 10. b4 $1 { White reinforces the pawn chain with b4, creating a solid structural foundation. This chain controls key squares and restricts the opponent's piece activity